    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0439" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1143</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-29T11:00:00+02:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 29, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 12:15 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>British Ambassador has just received a telegram from Cairo that Bedouins have
                    crossed frontier on their way to Suez Canal. He writes me it may mean war unless
                    his demand to the Grand Vizier to immediately withdraw Bedouins is complied
                    with.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
